OL,3,GNEWSACouncil defends progress on
OL,4,Avandal-hit playground
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe rebuilding of a play area torched
OL,7,Fby vandals remains on schedule,
OL,8,FBlackpool Council has said, after local
OL,9,Fcouncillors criticised delays.
OL,11,FThe play ship in Anchorsholme Park was
OL,12,Fdestroyed on 28 December, causing
OL,13,Fthousands of pounds worth of damage.
OL,15,FLocal Conservative councillors pledged
OL,16,Fto get the park's play area upgraded
OL,17,Fwith new equipment, and the Friends of
OL,18,FAnchorsholme Park charity committed
OL,19,F#10,000 towards the project.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
